    "type": "question",
    "label": "20",
    "prompt": "$g(x)=x-12$ and $h(x)=x^2-10$.\n\nSolve the equation $gh(x)=hg(x)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=6.5$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}gh(x)&=(x^2-10)-12\\\\&=x^2-22\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}hg(x)&=(x-12)^2-10\\\\&=x^2-24x+144-10\\\\&=x^2-24x+134\\end{align*}$$\nEquating the compositions:\n$$\\begin{align*}x^2-22&=x^2-24x+134\\\\24x&=156\\\\x&=6.5\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
